{
  "about": "What examples/plugins/recent-alerts does in a scripted run, recorded by crates/roster-core/tests/recent_alerts.rs (ROSTER_UPDATE_TRANSCRIPT=1 cargo test rewrites it). The fake Backend's stand-in replays it (recentAlerts.test.ts).",
  "steps": [
    {
      "config": {
        "leader": "w a",
        "patterns": [
          "ERROR",
          "panic"
        ]
      },
      "do": "load",
      "grants": [
        "terminal.read"
      ],
      "ops": [
        {
          "desc": "Recent alerts: :alerts shows them, :alerts clear dismisses them all",
          "name": "alerts",
          "op": "command",
          "run": "fn"
        },
        {
          "action": "finder alerts",
          "context": "leader",
          "keys": "w a",
          "op": "key"
        },
        {
          "id": "recent-alerts",
          "op": "help",
          "spec": {
            "markdown": "# Recent alerts\n\nWatches what your Sessions print and lists the lines with ERROR or panic in the **Recent alerts** section of the Sidebar, newest first, each with its Host and time.\n\n- `:alerts` shows them all; `:alerts clear` dismisses them all.\n- `␣ w a` finds one (`:finder alerts`); the status bar's `⚠` count opens the same finder.\n- On a row: Enter goes to the Host's Session; the buttons show the details, copy the line or dismiss it.\n\nIt keeps the last 100 alerts, in memory only: they're gone when the app restarts.\n\nIt needs **terminal.read**, which lets it see everything your Sessions print. Revoke it in `:plugins` and it stops at once.",
            "summary": "Lines your Sessions print that look like trouble",
            "title": "Recent alerts"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "recent-alerts",
          "op": "section",
          "spec": {
            "empty": "No alerts. Lines with ERROR or panic show here.",
            "order": 200,
            "rows": [],
            "title": "Recent alerts"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "alerts",
          "op": "finder",
          "spec": {
            "items": [],
            "title": "Recent alerts"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "alerts",
          "kind": "status",
          "op": "remove"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "do": "event",
      "name": "terminal_output",
      "ops": [
        {
          "id": "recent-alerts",
          "op": "section",
          "spec": {
            "empty": "No alerts. Lines with ERROR or panic show here.",
            "order": 200,
            "rows": [
              {
                "actions": [
                  {
                    "icon": "info",
                    "label": "Details of ERROR: disk /dev/sda1 full",
                    "run": "fn"
